RootED production migrations
============================

Run migrations from the repository root with the production virtual
environment active and `NGSS_DB` set to the absolute path of the existing
SQLite database. Use module invocation so repository imports resolve
consistently:

    python -m migrations.add_user_auth_identities --database "$NGSS_DB"
    python -m migrations.add_user_platform_roles
    python -m migrations.add_user_instructional_authorizations
    python -m migrations.add_account_lifecycle_and_objective_display
    python -m migrations.add_model_assets_table
    python -m migrations.add_student_growth_progress
    python -m migrations.add_student_question_deliveries
    python -m migrations.add_routing_level_attempts "$NGSS_DB"

Inspect production first and run only migrations that are pending. The required
dependency order for the recent adaptive schema is:

1. `student_growth_progress`
2. `student_question_deliveries`
3. `routing_level_attempts` and the accepted-response backfill

Never run these commands until the exact `NGSS_DB` path has been confirmed and
a readable production backup has been created.
